1
00:00:05,214 --> 00:00:07,674
[rain pattering]

2
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:10,385
[thunder rumbling]

3
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,517
[indistinct chatter]

4
00:00:27,486 --> 00:00:29,071
[clears throat]

5
00:00:44,503 --> 00:00:45,671
[Chang Ta-chin] Hmm...

6
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:48,674
Twice.

7
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:53,178
You've beaten up my son
twice at the school.

8
00:00:54,513 --> 00:00:57,349
I'm sorry about
what happened to your dad.

9
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:02,771
But you can't keep venting
your anger on my son, can you?

10
00:01:04,273 --> 00:01:05,482
What do you want?

11
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:09,235
[sighs]

12
00:01:09,236 --> 00:01:11,363
Your dad worked for me
for almost 30 years.

13
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:14,700
I respect him immensely.

14
00:01:14,825 --> 00:01:17,661
And I see you as my own son.

15
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:21,665
Seeing you like this
makes me sad.

16
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:25,168
If you're willing to admit
you're wrong

17
00:01:25,711 --> 00:01:30,715
and kneel down before me
and my son to bow
and make an apology,

18
00:01:30,716 --> 00:01:31,842
I'll forgive you.

19
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:33,467
[tense music playing]

20
00:01:33,468 --> 00:01:34,886
Hmm?

21
00:01:40,851 --> 00:01:42,561
[metal rattling]

22
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:49,651
It's you who should kneel down.

23
00:01:53,405 --> 00:01:54,614
[sighs]

24
00:01:54,615 --> 00:01:55,782
By the way,

25
00:01:56,783 --> 00:01:58,827
if you're in trouble again,

26
00:01:59,578 --> 00:02:00,912
use your brain.

27
00:02:01,163 --> 00:02:02,788
Don't rely on brute force
for everything.

28
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:04,416
[metal rattling]

29
00:02:05,584 --> 00:02:09,588
I'll never,
ever kneel down to you.

30
00:02:14,384 --> 00:02:17,387
Then you'll have
to stay in there to reflect
on what you've done.

31
00:02:17,888 --> 00:02:19,805
Remember what I've told you.

32
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:21,850
[laughing]

33
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:26,104
Thank you for
your hard work, sir.

34
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:27,230
[chuckles]

35
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:30,775
[secretary] <i>Wen has talked
to the police chief.</i>

36
00:02:30,776 --> 00:02:33,320
I've talked
to his public defender.

37
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:34,696
Don't worry, sir.

38
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:38,366
That boy is stubborn.

39
00:02:38,367 --> 00:02:41,328
He actually impressed me a lot.

40
00:02:43,497 --> 00:02:45,540
[birds chirping]

41
00:02:49,753 --> 00:02:52,838
You told me about the girl
who saw Chien-yuan's
license plate.

42
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:53,924
What is her name?

43
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:57,802
Her name, sir, is Wu Hsiu-wen.

44
00:02:57,803 --> 00:03:01,806
She's in the same class
as Chien-yuan.

45
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:04,308
Although we admitted
Chien-yuan is the car owner,

46
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:06,519
the investigation record states

47
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:08,980
our drunk driver took the car
without permission
and caused the accident.

48
00:03:09,231 --> 00:03:11,857
The girl's statement
means nothing.

49
00:03:11,858 --> 00:03:13,859
Don't worry, sir.

50
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:16,488
What's the relationship between
the girl and Chou Lu-yung?

51
00:03:17,823 --> 00:03:21,701
According to what we've
looked into, they're neighbors.

52
00:03:21,702 --> 00:03:23,620
And they've been
inseparable lately.

53
00:03:25,831 --> 00:03:27,374
[chuckles]

54
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,376
Inseparable?

55
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:33,422
[tense music playing]

56
00:03:37,843 --> 00:03:39,678
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

57
00:03:47,728 --> 00:03:50,521
We at Chang Xin
allocate a budget every year

58
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:51,815
for scholarships.

59
00:03:52,482 --> 00:03:56,903
An excellent student is who
we really want to reward.

60
00:03:57,988 --> 00:03:58,947
How's that?

61
00:04:01,533 --> 00:04:03,367
Thank you, sir,

62
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:05,579
but I've got enough money
for college tuition.

63
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:10,876
Even if you have enough
for tuition fees,
what about your living expenses?

64
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:14,421
And your grandma?

65
00:04:14,546 --> 00:04:16,631
Are you bringing her with you
to Taipei?

66
00:04:18,717 --> 00:04:20,218
Who'll take care of her?

67
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:22,721
If anything happens,
who'll be responsible?

68
00:04:27,309 --> 00:04:29,810
If you don't object to her going
to a long-term care center,

69
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:32,439
Chang Xin can assist you.

70
00:04:33,607 --> 00:04:35,692
[tense music fades in]

71
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:38,904
But...

72
00:04:39,029 --> 00:04:40,572
what price do I have to pay?

73
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:44,868
You want me to testify
against Chou Lu-yung?

74
00:04:47,746 --> 00:04:49,915
[laughing]

75
00:04:52,876 --> 00:04:54,752
Listen.

76
00:04:54,753 --> 00:04:56,922
I, Chang Da-chin,
never ask for anything
in return for my kindness.

77
00:04:57,047 --> 00:04:59,758
So, you don't have
to pay anything.

78
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:04,429
Hmm?

79
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:11,478
[singer] <i>♪ Someday, you can find
Sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

80
00:05:11,603 --> 00:05:15,940
[singing in Mandarin]

81
00:05:15,941 --> 00:05:17,901
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

82
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:20,070
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

83
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,446
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

84
00:05:22,447 --> 00:05:24,448
[singing in Mandarin]

85
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:28,495
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

86
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:33,375
[singing in Mandarin]

87
00:05:40,632 --> 00:05:43,009
[pensive music playing]

88
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:10,120
[music continues]

89
00:06:24,843 --> 00:06:25,844
Here's some fruit.

90
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:30,849
I heard that

91
00:06:31,558 --> 00:06:33,393
when Chang Xin's
stock price plummeted,

92
00:06:33,518 --> 00:06:35,645
you bought in with your dad's
life insurance payout.

93
00:06:36,021 --> 00:06:40,108
Besides, you inherited
your dad's shares
when he died, right?

94
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,071
I believe that in the long run,

95
00:06:45,196 --> 00:06:47,531
Chang Xin will be
a great company
with steady profits.

96
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:50,744
[laughing]

97
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:57,709
Before I came here,

98
00:06:58,919 --> 00:07:00,587
I expected so much from you.

99
00:07:00,712 --> 00:07:02,422
[tense music playing]

100
00:07:07,886 --> 00:07:09,471
I know you.

101
00:07:11,014 --> 00:07:12,807
Good job in marketing.

102
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:17,145
Thank you, sir.

103
00:07:17,938 --> 00:07:19,481
[chuckles]

104
00:07:23,068 --> 00:07:25,236
[Chang Ta-chin]
Here's some advice.

105
00:07:27,072 --> 00:07:29,240
Your food is not bad,

106
00:07:29,491 --> 00:07:31,242
but don't ever think
you can compete with us.

107
00:07:32,702 --> 00:07:34,578
With your dishes,

108
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:37,790
you're not good enough
to expand.

109
00:07:37,791 --> 00:07:38,917
It'll be hard work.

110
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:44,422
Don't worry.

111
00:07:44,547 --> 00:07:46,675
For your dad's sake,
I won't do anything to you.

112
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:54,933
I suggest
you stay in this small shop
to satisfy ordinary customers.

113
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:58,853
No problem at all
for you to earn a living.

114
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:01,231
Go for it.

115
00:08:05,986 --> 00:08:07,611
My goal is to defeat you.

116
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:09,655
[music intensifies]

117
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:11,157
It might be a long way to go,

118
00:08:12,534 --> 00:08:14,536
but I'll keep going forward
step by step.

119
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:17,122
You'll get older

120
00:08:17,247 --> 00:08:18,832
while I'll get stronger.

121
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:22,877
[Chien-yuan] What are you
talking about, Chou Lu-yung?

122
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:25,130
- You shut up!
- Don't tell me what to do.

123
00:08:25,255 --> 00:08:26,714
- Damn you!
- [glass shatters]

124
00:08:26,715 --> 00:08:27,798
- What?
- Come on!

125
00:08:27,799 --> 00:08:28,841
- Chien-yuan.
- You thug.

126
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:30,134
- [Chien-yuan] What?
- Chin-nan!

127
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:31,511
Let's fight!

128
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:32,804
- Come on!
- [Chin-nan] Bastard!

129
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:33,846
Chin-nan!

130
00:08:33,847 --> 00:08:36,891
[Chang Ta-chin laughing]

131
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:41,896
That boy of yours
really has guts.

132
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:44,566
I like him.

133
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:46,192
Good.

134
00:08:46,985 --> 00:08:48,153
I'll wait for you,

135
00:08:49,821 --> 00:08:51,740
but don't make me wait too long.

136
00:08:53,742 --> 00:08:55,702
[laughing]

137
00:08:56,745 --> 00:08:59,204
[tense music playing]

138
00:08:59,205 --> 00:09:00,331
[Chang Ta-chin sighs]

139
00:09:04,169 --> 00:09:07,338
[tense music playing]

140
00:09:15,889 --> 00:09:17,182
[Yi-hsuan] What's going on?

141
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:25,272
Chin-nan, you smashed a glass.
You think
you're still a gangster?

142
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:26,816
Fine.

143
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:28,026
I'm sorry.

144
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:31,696
[sighs]
You're sorry? What's the use?

145
00:09:33,031 --> 00:09:36,076
Will you take the responsibility
if we have to close down?
Can you afford it?

146
00:09:36,201 --> 00:09:38,369
She's right.
Why couldn't you hold back?

147
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:40,037
When I saw Chang Chien-yuan,

148
00:09:40,038 --> 00:09:41,873
I really wanted to spit
in the Three-cup Chicken.

149
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:44,751
But I didn't do it.

150
00:09:45,752 --> 00:09:46,711
I did.

151
00:09:47,879 --> 00:09:49,089
I spit once.

152
00:09:50,048 --> 00:09:50,924
[scoffs]

153
00:09:52,217 --> 00:09:53,885
Do you bear a grudge
against the Changs too, Feng?

154
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:55,803
No, I just don't like him,

155
00:09:55,804 --> 00:09:57,597
so I thickened his sauce
a little. [laughs]

156
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:02,143
I think you should
also hold back.

157
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:06,064
When the enemy is strong,
you can't challenge him
in public.

158
00:10:06,189 --> 00:10:08,775
He's not an easy opponent.

159
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,068
[chuckles]

160
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:13,780
He must think we're a bunch
of kids who can't even control
our tempers.

161
00:10:14,364 --> 00:10:15,740
What?

162
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:20,995
If he thinks so,
he won't bother
keeping an eye on us.

163
00:10:28,628 --> 00:10:30,713
[dramatic music playing]

164
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:39,931
LU-YUNG: TIME FOR YOU
TO KEEP YOUR PROMISE.

165
00:10:42,684 --> 00:10:45,728
[music continues]

166
00:10:50,316 --> 00:10:53,069
[rock music playing]

167
00:10:58,116 --> 00:11:02,286
[Lu-yung] <i>Someone once told me
not to rely only
on brute force,</i>

168
00:11:02,287 --> 00:11:04,664
<i>but to use my brain.</i>

169
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:06,958
<i>Back then,
he wanted to insult me.</i>

170
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:08,209
<i>But I listened.</i>

171
00:11:08,877 --> 00:11:10,794
<i>To defeat him,</i>

172
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:12,630
<i>I have to understand
what he's thinking.</i>

173
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:14,632
A DELICIOUS LIFE

174
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:16,259
<i>During my years in prison,</i>

175
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:18,385
<i>I read a lot about finance,</i>

176
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:21,263
<i>management,
and business operations.</i>

177
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:23,307
<i>Only by knowing yourself
and your enemy</i>

178
00:11:23,308 --> 00:11:24,267
<i>do you stand a chance
of winning.</i>

179
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:30,189
<i>The day I got out,
no one came to pick me up.</i>

180
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:31,899
<i>And I knew,</i>

181
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:33,443
<i>from that point on,</i>

182
00:11:33,693 --> 00:11:35,194
<i>I could only rely on myself.</i>

183
00:11:35,195 --> 00:11:38,239
[music continues]

184
00:11:39,991 --> 00:11:42,326
<i>Chang Xin Group,
the renowned restaurant giant,</i>

185
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:44,286
<i>has sparked
a cooking oil crisis,</i>

186
00:11:44,287 --> 00:11:45,872
<i>which upset the public.</i>

187
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:47,999
<i>Almost everybody in Taiwan
is in a rage.</i>

188
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:51,835
<i>An inside source has accused
the person in charge of the oil</i>

189
00:11:51,836 --> 00:11:54,714
<i>and their former R and D Chef,
Chou Jin-lai.</i>

190
00:11:54,839 --> 00:11:56,924
<i>He violated
the group's regulations</i>

191
00:11:56,925 --> 00:11:59,344
<i>and insisted on using
cheap, low-quality oil.</i>

192
00:11:59,928 --> 00:12:02,222
<i>Although Chou Jin-lai
has passed away,</i>

193
00:12:02,347 --> 00:12:04,974
<i>I'm fully responsible
for my poor judgment
in hiring him.</i>

194
00:12:05,767 --> 00:12:08,185
<i>We hereby sincerely
apologize to the public.</i>

195
00:12:08,186 --> 00:12:10,355
[camera clicking]

196
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:21,783
[pot boiling]

197
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:32,377
[stall owner] Hey!

198
00:12:34,045 --> 00:12:35,129
Your book.

199
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:38,341
Oh... I've memorized it.

200
00:12:39,384 --> 00:12:41,385
Please throw it away.

201
00:12:41,386 --> 00:12:42,387
Thank you!

202
00:12:44,514 --> 00:12:46,975
I'M WRONG

203
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:53,106
<i>I want to rebuild Jin Lai Hao,
restore my dad's reputation,</i>

204
00:12:53,856 --> 00:12:55,232
<i>and defeat Chang Xin.</i>

205
00:12:55,233 --> 00:12:57,902
[rock music playing]

206
00:13:09,414 --> 00:13:11,124
[Lu-yung]
<i>To achieve these goals,</i>

207
00:13:11,249 --> 00:13:12,583
<i>I need enough funding.</i>

208
00:13:14,085 --> 00:13:17,004
<i>I've been at sea
for four years,
working hard to save money.</i>

209
00:13:17,005 --> 00:13:18,339
[music continues]

210
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:25,305
[Lu-yung] <i>There aren't many
willing to fight alongside me.</i>

211
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:30,310
<i>But I know they'll be
waiting for me
when I come back.</i>

212
00:13:37,317 --> 00:13:40,445
[Lu-yung] <i>Finally,
I need a key partner,</i>

213
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:43,488
<i>someone who can turn
things around from the inside.</i>

214
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:45,283
[horn wailing]

215
00:13:49,829 --> 00:13:51,289
[Lu-yung] Thank you
for visiting my dad.

216
00:13:54,459 --> 00:13:57,002
[Shu-min] You disappeared
for four years
and have finally come back.

217
00:13:57,003 --> 00:13:58,963
What are you planning to do?

218
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:00,340
[Lu-yung] I've been planning
to open a restaurant.

219
00:14:01,341 --> 00:14:03,133
[Shu-min]
Your dad helped me a lot.

220
00:14:03,134 --> 00:14:04,844
Here's my advice.

221
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:07,137
If you're opening
a restaurant for him,

222
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:11,351
and not because you really
want to, then don't do it.

223
00:14:11,476 --> 00:14:15,520
Don't enter
the restaurant industry
out of spite.

224
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:17,023
[dramatic music playing]

225
00:14:17,148 --> 00:14:18,316
[sighs]

226
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:23,196
I want to help you.

227
00:14:23,654 --> 00:14:25,489
I want to get on
Chang Xin's board of directors

228
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:27,617
and help you
take over the company.

229
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:34,165
I know you're capable
like your dad used to be,

230
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:35,500
and enthusiastic too.

231
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:39,462
But the capital game
is something else.

232
00:14:41,464 --> 00:14:43,174
You can't help me much.

233
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:47,095
I have Chang Xin's shares.

234
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:49,389
3% of them.

235
00:14:51,516 --> 00:14:54,685
- Chou Jin-lai's shares?
- Yeah.

236
00:14:54,936 --> 00:14:57,145
When their stock price
plummeted,

237
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:59,607
I bought in with my dad's
life insurance payout.

238
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,526
Kind of ironic.

239
00:15:02,527 --> 00:15:04,612
Bet you never thought
I'm one of their
major shareholders?

240
00:15:10,076 --> 00:15:11,369
What do you want me to do?

241
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:17,208
[Lu-yung] <i>You're Chang Xin's
second largest shareholder.</i>

242
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:19,459
<i>I want you to lead the group.</i>

243
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,461
<i>If there's a motion
to remove the chairman,</i>

244
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:23,047
<i>I'll side with you.</i>

245
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:26,216
For me, even if you've inherited
your dad's shares,

246
00:15:26,217 --> 00:15:28,553
it's far from enough.

247
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:35,393
But you're Chou Jin-lai's son.
Maybe I can expect something
from you.

248
00:15:38,146 --> 00:15:39,897
I'll give you a task.

249
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:42,483
Get Chang Da-chin
to dine at your restaurant.

250
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:47,487
<i>To prove
he's really bothered by you</i>

251
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:48,948
<i>and your restaurant
is good enough</i>

252
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:50,658
<i>to attract his attention,</i>

253
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,411
<i>and you're qualified
to help me.</i>

254
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:57,081
Then I'll trust you.

255
00:15:57,206 --> 00:15:59,959
[pensive music playing]

256
00:16:03,671 --> 00:16:05,715
[birds chirping]

257
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:10,595
[Lu-yung] Hi, Miss Chiang.

258
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:15,391
Congratulations.
Mission accomplished.

259
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:19,103
I'll be your partner
from now on.

260
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:26,652
Let's do it.

261
00:16:26,777 --> 00:16:28,196
[birds chirping]

262
00:16:40,082 --> 00:16:41,292
It tastes better
with some vinegar.

263
00:16:49,383 --> 00:16:52,178
- Go get busy.
- Okay. Let's go.

264
00:17:01,187 --> 00:17:03,105
What? What is it?

265
00:17:08,444 --> 00:17:13,156
Well, sir, you often say
we're like brothers.

266
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:15,201
Yeah, sure. What else?

267
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:21,290
- Then I'll be straightforward.
- Go on.

268
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:25,710
Lately, my son keeps getting
respiratory tract infections.

269
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:29,382
I think I should
spend more time with him.

270
00:17:30,508 --> 00:17:33,594
I'm afraid I won't have
the capacity to take good care
of your affairs.

271
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:42,520
It sounds like
you need money for your son now.

272
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:45,689
Now the doctor is saying

273
00:17:45,690 --> 00:17:48,651
he can't guarantee
how much longer he'll live.

274
00:17:50,486 --> 00:17:52,279
Maybe five years.

275
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:53,322
Maybe ten days.

276
00:17:54,365 --> 00:17:56,033
[sighs] Damn!

277
00:17:56,158 --> 00:17:57,660
It's just fate.
What else can I do?

278
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:00,037
[sighs]

279
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:01,747
[tense music playing]

280
00:18:01,872 --> 00:18:05,543
In our line of work,
we have principles.

281
00:18:05,668 --> 00:18:09,296
What shouldn't be told,
I won't say a word.

282
00:18:09,297 --> 00:18:10,298
Don't worry.

283
00:18:16,721 --> 00:18:20,224
Wen, to be honest,

284
00:18:21,309 --> 00:18:22,893
I've never worried about you.

285
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:27,606
But you're
telling me this suddenly,
and I don't know what to do.

286
00:18:27,607 --> 00:18:28,733
I don't trust anyone else.

287
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:32,695
If you were me,
what would you do?

288
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:37,741
Here's the deal.

289
00:18:37,742 --> 00:18:39,242
For the time being,

290
00:18:39,243 --> 00:18:41,287
just take a break
to be with your son.

291
00:18:41,412 --> 00:18:43,747
When I need you, I'll call you.

292
00:18:43,748 --> 00:18:46,333
Whether you'll take
the job or not,
we'll discuss it then.

293
00:18:46,334 --> 00:18:47,460
Is that okay?

294
00:18:52,590 --> 00:18:54,884
Fine. It's a deal.

295
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:56,260
Thank you, sir.

296
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:59,430
[music continues]

297
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:10,775
[indistinct chatter]

298
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:12,818
[dramatic music playing]

299
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:15,780
- Hi, ma'am.
- [nurse] Morning.

300
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:21,243
[device beeping steadily]

301
00:19:36,175 --> 00:19:38,177
[music continues]

302
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:51,564
WHERE THERE'S LIFE,
THERE'S HOPE.

303
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:52,983
KEEP GOING.
MAKE SOME PROGRESS EVERY DAY.

304
00:19:53,234 --> 00:19:54,485
STAY STRONG! WE'RE ALL HERE.

305
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:55,695
WAKE UP.

306
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:57,154
GO FOR IT.

307
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:58,656
DON'T GIVE UP EASILY.

308
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:19,760
[dog barking in distance]

309
00:20:28,394 --> 00:20:29,854
[sighs]

310
00:20:37,987 --> 00:20:40,530
Are you still awake,
or did I wake you up?

311
00:20:40,531 --> 00:20:43,534
[Wen's son]
With all that loud banging,
who could possibly sleep?

312
00:20:49,415 --> 00:20:50,624
What's wrong with your cheek?

313
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:53,711
[microwave powers on]

314
00:20:54,962 --> 00:20:56,421
[Wen's son]
Bumped into something.

315
00:20:56,422 --> 00:20:58,799
Bumped into what
to make it look like that?

316
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:01,469
[Wen's son]
Just playing basketball.

317
00:21:15,316 --> 00:21:17,901
When you play basketball,
don't be so sissy.

318
00:21:17,902 --> 00:21:20,612
A sissy boy suffers easily.

319
00:21:20,613 --> 00:21:21,572
Understand?

320
00:21:28,454 --> 00:21:30,414
[Wen's son]
I think school is boring.

321
00:21:31,957 --> 00:21:33,833
What?

322
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:35,419
[timer dings]

323
00:21:49,058 --> 00:21:52,519
Dad, I don't want to go
to school.

324
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:54,104
Can I go to work now?

325
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:57,524
[sighs]

326
00:21:57,525 --> 00:21:58,567
There you go again.

327
00:21:59,652 --> 00:22:02,488
[phone buzzing]

328
00:22:02,613 --> 00:22:04,114
Fine. Go back to bed.

329
00:22:06,659 --> 00:22:08,953
[soft music playing]

330
00:22:12,456 --> 00:22:15,584
Hey, take the ointment with you.

331
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:25,970
[device beeping steadily]

332
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:34,019
JIN LAI HAO - REVIEWS

333
00:22:35,896 --> 00:22:37,647
[Yi-hsuan] Lin Chin-nan,

334
00:22:37,648 --> 00:22:39,483
you've been complained about.

335
00:22:39,984 --> 00:22:42,152
"Waited for a long time,
and nobody gave me a menu."

336
00:22:42,403 --> 00:22:44,696
"Service was slow too.
Not recommended."

337
00:22:44,697 --> 00:22:48,367
What the hell? I'm not Naruto.
I can't do shadow clones.

338
00:22:48,492 --> 00:22:50,034
[phone chimes]

339
00:22:50,035 --> 00:22:51,579
Here's another one.

340
00:22:52,454 --> 00:22:57,667
"What a bad restaurant!
Bad food and bad service.
Overrated."

341
00:22:57,668 --> 00:23:00,004
That's going too far.
Is our food that bad?

342
00:23:00,921 --> 00:23:03,340
They did it on purpose.

343
00:23:03,465 --> 00:23:05,467
Those difficult customers.

344
00:23:09,096 --> 00:23:11,723
I suspect someone paid
for those bad comments.

345
00:23:11,724 --> 00:23:14,058
[tense music playing]

346
00:23:14,059 --> 00:23:16,687
[indistinct chatter]

347
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:22,692
- [man] Hey, pal.
- Hey.

348
00:23:22,693 --> 00:23:24,527
[man] This is Gigi.

349
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:27,072
This is Cindy.

350
00:23:27,197 --> 00:23:30,034
My Cindy girl. [laughs]

351
00:23:30,159 --> 00:23:31,534
Hmm?

352
00:23:31,535 --> 00:23:34,997
Those bad comments look so real.

353
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:37,624
Amazing, huh? Let me tell you.

354
00:23:37,625 --> 00:23:40,043
You can't just leave
one-star comments.

355
00:23:40,044 --> 00:23:41,920
You have to mix in
some two or three-star ones

356
00:23:41,921 --> 00:23:43,464
to make it look real.

357
00:23:45,049 --> 00:23:46,049
Then I want more.

358
00:23:46,050 --> 00:23:47,467
[man] More?

359
00:23:47,468 --> 00:23:48,427
Okay.

360
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:51,971
Leave it to me. Don't worry.

361
00:23:51,972 --> 00:23:52,889
JIN LAI HAO
SEARCH

362
00:23:52,890 --> 00:23:54,641
JIN LAI HAO

363
00:23:54,642 --> 00:23:55,934
AVERAGE ENVIRONMENT,
SLOW SERVICE, AND COLD STAFF...

364
00:23:55,935 --> 00:23:57,185
THE FOOD IS BAD
AND IT'S EXPENSIVE AS HELL...

365
00:23:57,186 --> 00:23:58,144
DEFINITELY AN OVERRATED
INFLUENCER TRAP.

366
00:23:58,145 --> 00:23:59,229
SERVER IS LONG-FACED...

367
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:00,647
BAD ATTITUDE, MESSY,
SLOW SERVICE...

368
00:24:00,648 --> 00:24:03,567
We can't let
online reviews define us.

369
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:05,944
We need to become
an iconic restaurant.

370
00:24:05,945 --> 00:24:08,614
You need to become
an iconic chef.

371
00:24:08,739 --> 00:24:10,657
Look at those
famous restaurants.

372
00:24:10,658 --> 00:24:12,784
They get one-star comments
sometimes.

373
00:24:12,785 --> 00:24:14,870
But they don't need
to give a damn.

374
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:18,832
I'll do my best.

375
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:21,919
You don't look anxious at all.

376
00:24:24,213 --> 00:24:25,214
But I'm anxious.

377
00:24:26,757 --> 00:24:28,926
When you are anxious,
what do you do?

378
00:24:30,135 --> 00:24:33,597
I work hard
to do what I'm supposed to do.

379
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:38,686
What's wrong?

380
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:42,648
You're mature and annoying.

381
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:49,028
I want you
to have some weaknesses
to show that I'm important.

382
00:24:49,029 --> 00:24:51,115
[light music playing]

383
00:24:53,117 --> 00:24:54,785
But you are important.

384
00:24:54,910 --> 00:24:57,121
Really? How many stars
would you give me?

385
00:24:58,789 --> 00:25:01,165
From one to five. How many?

386
00:25:01,166 --> 00:25:02,793
Didn't you say I'm important?

387
00:25:03,877 --> 00:25:05,671
You're really important.

388
00:25:05,796 --> 00:25:08,798
You guys and the restaurant
mean everything to me.

389
00:25:08,799 --> 00:25:10,134
I don't need to give you stars.

390
00:25:10,259 --> 00:25:11,802
You're so lame.

391
00:25:11,927 --> 00:25:13,678
You should say

392
00:25:13,679 --> 00:25:16,265
I'm your star
in the darkness of the night.

393
00:25:19,810 --> 00:25:20,894
[clicks tongue]

394
00:25:21,854 --> 00:25:22,980
You fool!

395
00:25:26,734 --> 00:25:28,277
You're so annoying.

396
00:25:28,527 --> 00:25:31,905
My star
in the darkness of the night?
Is there a power outage?

397
00:25:35,242 --> 00:25:37,286
[moaning and groaning]

398
00:25:44,668 --> 00:25:45,753
[sighs]

399
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:49,840
[keypad tapping]

400
00:25:51,341 --> 00:25:53,677
I'M SUDDENLY EMOTIONAL.

401
00:25:53,802 --> 00:25:57,848
BUT SOMEONE DOESN'T EVEN KNOW
WHAT THAT MEANS.

402
00:26:02,352 --> 00:26:03,645
[sighs]

403
00:26:04,855 --> 00:26:05,939
[phone chimes]

404
00:26:12,613 --> 00:26:15,740
CHIEN-WU: I FOUND OUT WHO PAID
FOR THOSE BAD COMMENTS.

405
00:26:15,741 --> 00:26:18,034
MY BROTHER...

406
00:26:18,035 --> 00:26:20,746
YI-HSUAN: YEAH, I THOUGHT SO.

407
00:26:20,871 --> 00:26:25,751
HOW DARE HE?
I'LL MAKE HIM PAY.

408
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:31,924
[Chang Ta-chin]
This is the latest beef

409
00:26:32,049 --> 00:26:34,051
from the U.S. Meat
Export Federation.

410
00:26:34,176 --> 00:26:35,677
It's cheap,

411
00:26:36,303 --> 00:26:37,888
and can be cooked in many ways.

412
00:26:38,013 --> 00:26:39,890
You can even use it for steak.

413
00:26:40,015 --> 00:26:41,809
Let's see if it works
for our beef soup this time.

414
00:26:46,105 --> 00:26:47,772
Tastes good.

415
00:26:47,773 --> 00:26:50,024
It really works well.
Which cut is it?

416
00:26:50,025 --> 00:26:52,110
The sirloin tip.

417
00:26:52,111 --> 00:26:53,737
They call it knuckle beef.

418
00:26:54,238 --> 00:26:55,781
It's very lean.

419
00:26:55,906 --> 00:26:57,741
They used to make
ground beef with it.

420
00:26:57,866 --> 00:27:00,243
But recently beef prices
have been getting higher
and higher.

421
00:27:00,244 --> 00:27:02,161
So, the Americans
have figured out a way

422
00:27:02,162 --> 00:27:08,043
to use low-fat
as a selling point to rebrand
this cheap cut of meat.

423
00:27:09,086 --> 00:27:10,254
The Americans are so smart.

424
00:27:11,755 --> 00:27:14,883
They always find a way to export
their garbage to the world.

425
00:27:16,260 --> 00:27:17,970
We need to step up our game.

426
00:27:20,639 --> 00:27:22,057
[laughs]

427
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:32,818
Shu-min?

428
00:27:35,654 --> 00:27:37,781
I need to ask you a question.

429
00:27:39,950 --> 00:27:41,076
Okay.

430
00:27:44,288 --> 00:27:46,665
Chien-yuan and Chien-wu,

431
00:27:46,790 --> 00:27:49,167
who do you think is more suited
to be my successor?

432
00:27:49,168 --> 00:27:51,253
[tense music playing]

433
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:03,640
I think they're both capable,

434
00:28:03,765 --> 00:28:07,269
but they're still young
and need your guidance.

435
00:28:10,814 --> 00:28:12,398
But if you ask me,

436
00:28:12,399 --> 00:28:14,318
I think it should be you.

437
00:28:19,364 --> 00:28:21,491
[chuckles]

438
00:28:21,742 --> 00:28:25,870
Uncle, it's a trend
for enterprises to hire
professional managers.

439
00:28:25,871 --> 00:28:29,458
Don't push Chien-yuan
and Chien-wu too hard.

440
00:28:29,708 --> 00:28:31,042
Give them some time.

441
00:28:31,043 --> 00:28:32,502
You'll see their potential.

442
00:28:39,509 --> 00:28:41,345
[laughs]

443
00:28:41,470 --> 00:28:43,847
Fine. Let's have the soup.

444
00:28:43,972 --> 00:28:46,141
[pensive music playing]

445
00:29:11,917 --> 00:29:14,126
- Are you almost done?
- Yeah.

446
00:29:14,127 --> 00:29:16,003
I'll cook
our midnight snacks then.

447
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:17,922
Let's have stir-fried
beef noodles today.

448
00:29:17,923 --> 00:29:19,508
[both] Sounds great.

449
00:29:19,758 --> 00:29:22,261
We've worked hard enough
to deserve some beef
from the restaurant.

450
00:29:22,386 --> 00:29:23,512
Right?

451
00:29:23,762 --> 00:29:25,264
I'll tell Boss.

452
00:29:25,389 --> 00:29:29,100
Boss says, "It's okay."

453
00:29:29,101 --> 00:29:31,353
[laughter]

454
00:29:38,235 --> 00:29:41,905
This dish needs plenty of oil.
Don't spare it.

455
00:29:45,242 --> 00:29:47,077
Put them in
when it's hot enough.

456
00:29:47,202 --> 00:29:49,288
[sizzling]

457
00:29:51,039 --> 00:29:53,291
Stir-fry is all about
high heat and speed.

458
00:29:53,292 --> 00:29:55,251
You need to control the heat,

459
00:29:55,252 --> 00:29:57,587
get the oil hot
and stir-fry them
fast to create <i>wok hei</i> .

460
00:29:59,256 --> 00:30:00,424
See?

461
00:30:04,177 --> 00:30:06,262
No big deal. It's easy.

462
00:30:06,263 --> 00:30:07,973
I've made
stir-fried sticky rice.

463
00:30:09,057 --> 00:30:13,186
Without the right heat
or enough speed,
it'll never taste good.

464
00:30:15,272 --> 00:30:16,940
Don't delay once you add
the chives in.

465
00:30:29,828 --> 00:30:31,246
Looks delicious.

466
00:30:36,335 --> 00:30:39,170
[neighbor] Do not feed
stray cats to prevent
bacterial growth.

467
00:30:39,171 --> 00:30:43,425
[Yu-li] Sorry, but I'll get
those cats neutered to prevent
them from giving birth.

468
00:30:44,426 --> 00:30:47,137
[neighbor] Fine.
The sooner, the better.

469
00:30:47,262 --> 00:30:50,182
[Yu-li] Thank you,
you're so kind. Love you!

470
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:46,530
[exhales]

471
00:31:47,447 --> 00:31:51,368
Do you see me as a girl?

472
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:02,879
I had always been
called a sissy,

473
00:32:03,004 --> 00:32:05,340
bullied and excluded.

474
00:32:05,465 --> 00:32:07,008
Until I met Lu-yung,

475
00:32:08,677 --> 00:32:13,222
I realized someone in this world
was willing to understand me.

476
00:32:13,223 --> 00:32:15,558
[emotional music playing]

477
00:32:15,559 --> 00:32:19,604
I worked hard to save
200,000 dollars for him
to open a restaurant.

478
00:32:21,231 --> 00:32:23,233
But he asked me
to get the surgery.

479
00:32:24,317 --> 00:32:28,155
He said being myself
makes me free.

480
00:32:30,407 --> 00:32:31,658
Do you dare?

481
00:32:33,243 --> 00:32:35,453
It's not like cutting off
a finger.

482
00:32:35,454 --> 00:32:37,080
It's cutting...

483
00:32:37,205 --> 00:32:38,622
cutting off your junk.

484
00:32:38,623 --> 00:32:40,959
Yeah. Do you dare?

485
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:43,128
No way.

486
00:32:49,259 --> 00:32:50,719
To be a girl,

487
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:55,182
I've worked harder
than any girl in the world.

488
00:32:58,268 --> 00:32:59,603
Even so,

489
00:33:01,688 --> 00:33:03,440
you still think I'm weird?

490
00:33:06,651 --> 00:33:12,324
I thought it wasn't fair
that I was the only one
who didn't know.

491
00:33:12,449 --> 00:33:14,326
Because you're stupid.

492
00:33:14,451 --> 00:33:16,119
Only you couldn't tell.

493
00:33:18,121 --> 00:33:20,290
You're lovely.
Of course, I couldn't tell.

494
00:33:23,001 --> 00:33:25,128
I said you're lovely.
Of course, I couldn't tell.

495
00:33:27,130 --> 00:33:29,299
What? I can't hear you.

496
00:33:30,634 --> 00:33:33,136
You're lovely.
Of course, I couldn't tell.

497
00:33:37,474 --> 00:33:40,518
Tsai? Heard that?

498
00:33:40,519 --> 00:33:42,728
You are my witness.

499
00:33:42,729 --> 00:33:44,648
He said I'm lovely.

500
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:50,152
Fine.

501
00:33:50,153 --> 00:33:51,446
Still my best boy.

502
00:33:55,325 --> 00:33:56,243
My best girl.

503
00:33:57,536 --> 00:34:00,455
Whatever. My best boy and girl.

504
00:34:01,331 --> 00:34:04,209
[cat purrs and meows]

505
00:34:11,132 --> 00:34:12,217
Have a seat.

506
00:34:15,720 --> 00:34:18,180
You're such a young
district manager,

507
00:34:18,181 --> 00:34:19,682
and even in charge
of brand planning.

508
00:34:19,683 --> 00:34:21,559
It's not easy.

509
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:23,562
Because you taught me well.

510
00:34:24,229 --> 00:34:25,355
That's true.

511
00:34:26,356 --> 00:34:27,356
Have some tea.

512
00:34:27,357 --> 00:34:28,525
Thank you.

513
00:34:36,741 --> 00:34:39,828
I've got a new brand.

514
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:41,704
Its target audience
is young people.

515
00:34:41,705 --> 00:34:46,208
So, I need an innovative
and reliable manager

516
00:34:46,209 --> 00:34:47,793
to be in charge of it.

517
00:34:47,794 --> 00:34:50,171
And I think
you're the right person.

518
00:34:57,137 --> 00:34:59,889
- It does sound
like a good chance.
- Come back to help me.

519
00:35:02,100 --> 00:35:04,227
I want you to stand by me.

520
00:35:04,352 --> 00:35:05,729
You'll need to choose
sooner or later.

521
00:35:12,235 --> 00:35:15,404
But, Miss Chiang,
I don't think I'm good enough.

522
00:35:15,405 --> 00:35:17,407
I need to learn more
at the headquarters.

523
00:35:20,285 --> 00:35:21,578
Are you saying no to me?

524
00:35:25,415 --> 00:35:27,292
I'm not mature enough.

525
00:35:27,417 --> 00:35:29,794
I need to learn more
to really help you.

526
00:35:37,594 --> 00:35:39,470
Yeah, fine.
Go home and think about it.

527
00:35:39,471 --> 00:35:41,348
If you have any thoughts,
just tell me.

528
00:35:42,515 --> 00:35:45,809
Besides, don't think
about work all the time.

529
00:35:45,810 --> 00:35:47,562
You don't have
a boyfriend, do you?

530
00:35:49,606 --> 00:35:52,650
But I don't have time for that.

531
00:35:52,651 --> 00:35:55,362
I know a nice guy.
Should I introduce him to you?

532
00:35:56,321 --> 00:35:59,783
Since you joined us,
I've never seen you dating.

533
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:05,664
We'll see.
We've been so busy lately.

534
00:36:07,874 --> 00:36:10,376
I'm glad you're enterprising.

535
00:36:10,377 --> 00:36:12,837
But sometimes
falling in love is good for you.

536
00:36:14,297 --> 00:36:15,381
Yeah.

537
00:36:15,382 --> 00:36:16,925
[thunder rumbles]

538
00:36:38,697 --> 00:36:39,864
[phone chimes]

539
00:36:43,910 --> 00:36:47,371
CHIEN-WU: ARE YOU AVAILABLE NOW?
I'M ANXIOUS ABOUT STUDYING
ABROAD.

540
00:36:47,372 --> 00:36:48,456
CAN WE TALK?

541
00:36:49,833 --> 00:36:51,626
[light music playing]

542
00:36:52,794 --> 00:36:53,837
[phone chimes]

543
00:36:57,590 --> 00:36:59,883
HSIU-WEN: WE'LL TALK
IN THE OFFICE, OKAY?

544
00:36:59,884 --> 00:37:01,886
[sighs]

545
00:37:11,646 --> 00:37:13,648
[singer singing in Mandarin]

546
00:37:14,357 --> 00:37:15,859
You're all I've got...

547
00:37:45,972 --> 00:37:47,432
I think you're...

548
00:37:51,394 --> 00:37:52,437
dazzling.

549
00:37:53,062 --> 00:37:55,064
[music continues]

550
00:38:01,321 --> 00:38:03,364
[singer] <i>♪ After everything ♪</i>

551
00:38:04,991 --> 00:38:08,577
<i>♪ Love is whispering... ♪</i>

552
00:38:08,578 --> 00:38:11,580
You're working
for the rival of my boss.

553
00:38:11,581 --> 00:38:14,542
How could you still
be his friend?

554
00:38:17,420 --> 00:38:21,006
[singer]
<i>♪ Just one more minute ♪</i>

555
00:38:21,007 --> 00:38:25,010
<i>♪ You will fade from memory ♪</i>

556
00:38:25,011 --> 00:38:26,930
[singing in Mandarin]

557
00:38:29,349 --> 00:38:31,017
[door buzzes and opens]

558
00:38:43,696 --> 00:38:46,115
What happened to your face?
Does it hurt?

559
00:38:46,366 --> 00:38:47,492
I'm fine.

560
00:38:49,661 --> 00:38:51,621
Thanks for coming
all the way to visit me.

561
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:57,335
What's going on?

562
00:39:00,964 --> 00:39:02,131
[chuckles]

563
00:39:05,677 --> 00:39:07,345
I got into college,

564
00:39:09,931 --> 00:39:11,474
a national one...

565
00:39:15,979 --> 00:39:17,355
in Taipei.

566
00:39:19,065 --> 00:39:21,067
That's great. Congratulations.

567
00:39:28,825 --> 00:39:30,535
Why don't you look happy?

568
00:39:33,746 --> 00:39:35,748
[music continues]

569
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:44,548
[Hsiu-wen] <i>Because Chang Xin</i>

570
00:39:44,549 --> 00:39:46,718
<i>is paying for my tuition
and living expenses...</i>

571
00:39:53,474 --> 00:39:57,562
and they put my grandma
in a long-term care center.

572
00:40:01,399 --> 00:40:03,026
Maybe they gave me all this

573
00:40:06,070 --> 00:40:08,698
because I called the police
to stop you.

574
00:40:21,628 --> 00:40:26,841
She works hard to do the job
she wants and lead the life
she wants.

575
00:40:29,886 --> 00:40:31,137
I respect her a lot.

576
00:40:34,891 --> 00:40:37,226
[dramatic music playing]

577
00:40:49,656 --> 00:40:50,740
I'm sorry.

578
00:40:54,994 --> 00:40:56,079
I'm so sorry.

579
00:40:58,539 --> 00:40:59,832
I'm not strong enough.

580
00:41:04,462 --> 00:41:05,588
I'm a coward.

581
00:41:06,965 --> 00:41:09,676
I can't be as brave as you.
I'm sorry.

582
00:41:10,802 --> 00:41:12,720
I'm sorry, Lu-yung.

583
00:41:13,763 --> 00:41:15,597
[sniffles]

584
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:17,642
[sobs]

585
00:41:25,274 --> 00:41:26,693
I'm grateful to you.

586
00:41:31,197 --> 00:41:32,782
If you hadn't stopped me,

587
00:41:34,617 --> 00:41:37,161
I would be a murderer,

588
00:41:37,286 --> 00:41:38,997
not just an attempted one.

589
00:41:46,212 --> 00:41:47,714
I want to thank you

590
00:41:48,840 --> 00:41:50,675
for bravely standing
in front of that gun...

591
00:41:51,175 --> 00:41:53,176
So annoying!

592
00:41:53,177 --> 00:41:55,804
[Lu-yung] <i>...so that I can be
sitting here, alive and well.</i>

593
00:41:55,805 --> 00:41:57,222
Stop blaming yourself.

594
00:41:57,223 --> 00:41:58,682
So annoying!

595
00:41:58,683 --> 00:42:00,226
[Lu-yung] You've done
nothing wrong.

596
00:42:01,644 --> 00:42:02,979
So annoying!

597
00:42:04,147 --> 00:42:06,649
- [door buzzes]
- [prison guard] Time's up!

598
00:42:09,569 --> 00:42:11,194
I've got to go.

599
00:42:11,195 --> 00:42:12,822
Thanks for visiting me.

600
00:42:17,660 --> 00:42:18,703
[groans]

601
00:42:19,287 --> 00:42:20,163
<i>Lu-yung?</i>

602
00:42:32,633 --> 00:42:33,760
Do you...

603
00:42:36,054 --> 00:42:37,638
still think I'm dazzling?

604
00:42:45,354 --> 00:42:46,647
Yeah, very much so.

605
00:42:53,696 --> 00:42:55,364
[indistinct chatter]

606
00:42:57,033 --> 00:42:59,202
[dramatic music playing]

607
00:43:05,875 --> 00:43:07,001
[door buzzes]

608
00:43:09,045 --> 00:43:10,296
[sighs]

609
00:43:12,882 --> 00:43:13,966
Lu-yung?

610
00:43:15,843 --> 00:43:17,220
[Chin-nan] His girlfriend.

611
00:43:23,684 --> 00:43:26,270
Do you think I'm an annoying
goddamn bitch?

612
00:43:27,188 --> 00:43:28,856
How could I do this to you?

613
00:43:30,066 --> 00:43:31,192
Right?

614
00:43:38,116 --> 00:43:40,159
Maybe you'll go without me.

615
00:43:41,244 --> 00:43:42,370
[Hsiu-wen] Is that right?

616
00:43:45,414 --> 00:43:46,707
[Chin-nan] Hi, Mrs. Chou.

617
00:43:55,800 --> 00:43:57,635
I've been hiding from you.

618
00:43:58,261 --> 00:44:00,263
[soft music playing]

619
00:44:06,727 --> 00:44:09,981
Actually, I'd like to know
how you've got so many customers
suddenly?

620
00:44:12,024 --> 00:44:13,359
Can you tell me?

621
00:44:14,944 --> 00:44:16,320
We're friends, aren't we?

622
00:44:22,243 --> 00:44:24,120
Because I found
a capable manager.

623
00:44:24,245 --> 00:44:26,247
[chuckles]

624
00:44:28,124 --> 00:44:29,959
You mean, that young girl?

625
00:44:31,335 --> 00:44:32,878
Come on. You're drunk.
I'll walk you home.

626
00:44:32,879 --> 00:44:34,005
Let go!

627
00:44:42,388 --> 00:44:44,140
I don't feel sorry
for you at all.

628
00:44:46,184 --> 00:44:48,728
I love myself. Am I wrong?

629
00:44:49,729 --> 00:44:50,897
Am I wrong?

630
00:44:53,733 --> 00:44:55,818
- Of course, you're not.
- There you go.

631
00:44:55,943 --> 00:44:58,112
I hate it when you act
like you know everything.

632
00:45:01,199 --> 00:45:03,326
You're a dropout
and an ex-convict.

633
00:45:05,077 --> 00:45:06,996
You're really annoying me.

634
00:45:08,706 --> 00:45:10,750
You're really annoying me.

635
00:45:15,004 --> 00:45:18,216
I'm sorry
for making you so upset.

636
00:45:22,428 --> 00:45:26,307
You're doing your best
to enjoy your life.
You've done nothing wrong.

637
00:45:30,102 --> 00:45:32,230
Don't talk to me like that.

638
00:45:35,107 --> 00:45:36,859
Don't talk like that.

639
00:45:40,446 --> 00:45:43,282
[singer singing in Mandarin]

640
00:45:44,033 --> 00:45:45,368
To be honest...

641
00:45:50,539 --> 00:45:51,999
I've always...

642
00:46:03,010 --> 00:46:04,553
always...

643
00:46:19,819 --> 00:46:21,403
[car horn blows]

644
00:46:21,404 --> 00:46:22,989
[grunts]

645
00:46:24,407 --> 00:46:27,201
[whimsical music playing]

646
00:46:31,080 --> 00:46:34,125
[credits music playing]
